.TH Prototyper 1 "October 2026" "CLAM" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
Prototyper \- runs CLAM networks with QML or Qt Designer interfaces
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B Prototyper
[Network.clamnetwork [Interface.qml|Interface.ui]]
[-o] [--start-paused] [-b backend [-b backend]...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Prototyper runs audio processing networks created by CLAM NetworkEditor.
QML interfaces import CLAM.Widgets 1.0 for audio monitors, controls and
playback helpers. Legacy Qt Designer .ui interfaces are also supported.
.PP
When no interface path is supplied, Prototyper tries a .qml file with the
same basename as the network, then a .ui file, then its built-in interface.
An explicitly supplied interface must load and bind successfully.
.PP
QML monitors use clamOutPort properties containing Processing.Port names.
Controls use clamInControl or clamOutControl with Processing.Control names.
QML control ranges are specified in control units. Legacy .ui interfaces
retain the widget naming and property conventions of the Qt binders.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -b backend
Try an audio backend. Repeat to provide a preference order. Supported
backends are jack and portaudio, when enabled at build time.
Without this option they are tried in that order.
.TP
.B -o
Run without an interface. Requires a network file.
.TP
.B --start-paused
Wait for Play before processing audio.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Print usage information and exit.
.SH AUTHOR
CLAM development team
.SH SEE ALSO
NetworkEditor(1), OfflinePlayer(1), CheckClamNetwork(1)
.PP
See NetworkEditor/QML-WIDGETS.md in the source tree for QML authoring,
preview tool setup and the component migration table.
